From: Giovanni Ricciardi IU1WXY <info@x6100-link.it>
Subject: [PATCH] enable protected management frames (802.11w)

The driver carries the PMF code (BIP/AES-CMAC, SA Query, protected
deauth/disassoc) under CONFIG_IEEE80211W, but the Makefile never
defined it. With it on, AES-CMAC is listed in the cipher suites, so
wpa_supplicant sees BIP support and uses PMF with routers that offer
or require it. omac1_aes_128() is also called from rtw_xmit.c, so it
cannot stay static.

Signed-off-by: Giovanni Ricciardi IU1WXY <info@x6100-link.it>
---
diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 611160e..a924f16 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-unused-parameter
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-unused-function
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-unused
 #EXTRA_CFLAGS += -DCONFIG_CONCURRENT_MODE
+EXTRA_CFLAGS += -DCONFIG_IEEE80211W
 
 ccflags-y += -D__CHECK_ENDIAN__
 
diff --git a/core/rtw_security.c b/core/rtw_security.c
index 07f021d..f043799 100644
--- a/core/rtw_security.c
+++ b/core/rtw_security.c
@@ -2898,7 +2898,7 @@ static int omac1_aes_128_vector(u8 *key, size_t num_elem,
  * OMAC1 was standardized with the name CMAC by NIST in a Special Publication
  * (SP) 800-38B.
  */ //modify for CONFIG_IEEE80211W
-static int omac1_aes_128(u8 *key, u8 *data, size_t data_len, u8 *mac)
+int omac1_aes_128(u8 *key, u8 *data, size_t data_len, u8 *mac)
 {
 	return omac1_aes_128_vector(key, 1, &data, &data_len, mac);
 }
